The desk merged **412 reports** into #4471 as one date bug. The table below, which the kb
computes from the reports and the tenant directory, shows two causes.

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## What each cause is

- **parser (379 reports):** the shared parser reads dates month first. Tenants that write the
  day first get flipped dates. This is the bug #4471 describes. 5 of these read as a one-day
  move; the desk files them under parser by tenant.
- **hint (33 reports):** all via the booking form of tenants on booking-v3 (alder.physio,
  copper.studio, pale.harbour). The form prints MM/DD/YYYY under the date field, so people type
  month first and the form reads it day first. A parser fix does not change this.

<Callout>
Not one issue. A parser fix closes 379 reports. The other 33 need the booking-v3 hint changed.
</Callout>

## Why intake tags mislead

Intake guesses from the browser locale. It tagged 15 of the 33 hint reports as parser.
Cause depends on the tenant and its form, so count from `causeOf` in `causes.ts`, not from tags.

<RenderStamp {signature} />
